            <ArticleTitle>A one pot three-component reaction for the preparation of dihydroquinolines with two different ketones and aromatic amines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10167-10171</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02554h</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A three component reaction with two different ketones and aromatic amines was firstly investigated. The difference in reactivity between ordinary ketones and ketone esters allowed for the production of 1,2-DHQs efficiently. The possible Skraup reaction with 2 equiv. of the same ketones was prohibited due to the fast formation of imines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
